message: "If you use this research, please cite the paper and this repository."
title: "The Persistence Ceiling: Testing Whether Form, Tournaments, and Squad Value Improve National-Team Elo Forecasts"
abstract: >-
  National-team federations routinely read recent form, tournament performance,
  volatility, and squad value as signs that a team may be rising or fading. This
  study separates the LEVEL, DIRECTION and ERROR roles of those signals by
  testing the additional out-of-time forecasting information carried by richer
  historical signals when current Elo is already known, on a frozen
  national-team-season panel covering 1980-2026.
